# Diva ttyds answer init for 7950 on controller 4: one port, either bearer.
#
# TTY profile 14 autodetects the incoming B-channel protocol (AT.txt,
# Supported TTY Profiles), so this tty accepts an analog modem call and a
# digital 64k call on the same number. The modem settings below apply to the
# analog case; they are the same ones the 79x0 modem answerers use.
#
# AT+iF5 is the RNA framing converter: "detects required conversation by
# analyzing incoming data packets". A digital call carries synchronous HDLC
# PPP on the B channel, while pppd on the ttyds port speaks async PPP, so
# without this the answer direction arrives as synchronous HDLC. With it the
# card converts, and both bearers reach pppd as async PPP.
ABORT 'ERROR'
TIMEOUT 5
'' '\dAT&F14'
OK 'AT+iQ=a4'
OK 'AT+iA7950'
OK 'AT+MS=V90,1'
OK 'AT\\N3%C1'
OK 'AT+iF5'
OK 'ATE0V1S0=1\\V1#CID=14'
REPORT CONNECT
TIMEOUT 86400
CONNECT '\c'
'\n' '\c'
